 "text": "Hey, nice to hear from you. How's life treating you? It' making the bike comfortable for you. The saddle height, distance from the ground, and angle, the handlebars and whether you lean forward. Sounds like you. The shop will have a comfortable bike for you. Then a shorter reach handlebar with drop Bars can help. A shop will make sure it' set up right, so it' worth it. Not usually. A proper bike fit costs about £50. A quick check is worth a few minutes, but it only gets you so far. A proper fit takes an hour.",
